INT. MOVING VAN - DAY

CLOSE ON the back of a rattling box truck, packed to the roof with old furniture wrapped in grey blankets. We see a walnut dresser from the 1920s, a mirror in a gilded frame, and a tall grandfather clock lashed with orange straps.

Rain hammers on the metal roof. The road outside is wet and grey. It is a very dull morning.

SAM, 30s, sits on a crate near the back door, looking worried. He checks the straps again. Next to him JEN, 20s, is writing on a clipboard. In the front, through a little window, we see BIG DAVE driving and MO in the passenger seat eating chips.

SAM
Jen, are you sure the clock is secure? It's worth like ten thousand dollars.

JEN
He has checked it three times, Sam. He is very sure.

SAM
I'm just saying, if it falls, we all lose our jobs.

The van hits a pothole. The clock RATTLES. The mirror TINKLES. She grabs the clipboard. He grabs the clock.

BIG DAVE (O.S.)
Sorry about that, folks!

MO (O.S.)
(through the window)
Dave, watch the road!

Lightning FLASHES through the cracks in the door and, for a second, we see everyone's faces lit up in white.

In the back, behind the dresser, a hand moves. It is an old woman's hand, wrinkled and thin, and she pushes a blanket aside. This is MRS. K, 80s, the owner of all this furniture, who has been hiding in the van the whole time.

SAM
(shocked)
Mrs. K?

MRS. K
I wasn't going to let you take Henry's clock without me.

JEN
Ma'am, you can't be back here. It's not safe.

MRS. K
I have been safe for eighty years. I would like to be something else.

The phone in Jen's pocket BUZZES. She looks at it, he looks at her, and she answers.

JEN
(into phone)
Hello? Yes, we have her. No, she's fine.

LOU (V.O.)
(over phone)
Jen, it's Lou at dispatch. The client's daughter just called. Her mother is missing. Please tell me she's in the van.

JEN
She is in the van.

LOU (V.O.)
Oh thank God.

The van HONKS and SCREECHES to a halt. Everyone slides forward. The clock tips. Sam catches it, barely. They all breathe.

A pause. The rain softens. Out the back window a rainbow, small and surprised, appears over a wet parking lot.

MRS. K
(smiling)
Henry always loved a rainbow.

Sam looks at her. She looks at him. They both understand something they cannot say.

BIG DAVE (O.S.)
We're here! Everybody out!

The back door RATTLES OPEN. Light pours in.
